new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4788651
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apt/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+
+## Individual shared libraries
+
+`apt.install` exports each development package's unversioned `libNAME.so` as
+`@packages//package-dev:libNAME_cc`. This native C/C++ target supplies one shared
+library, the package's public headers, and declared runtime linker inputs. Other
+libraries from the same package are available to resolve runtime dependencies
+without being added as direct link libraries. The existing package-level library
+and `_headers` targets retain their interfaces.
+
+For link options requiring an explicitly ordered library filename,
+`@packages//package-dev:libNAME_shared` supplies that one file. Both targets select
+the requested target architecture. For transitional development packages, consume
+the development package that actually owns the library. Runtime-only locked
+imports continue to expose archive inputs without C/C++ exports.
+
+The runtime closure reuses each package's existing `_so_libs` interface. Its
+empty interface libraries keep runtime-only files out of direct `DT_NEEDED`
+entries, while their declared SONAME filenames enter Bazel's solib directories
+and runtime search paths. Plain `data` files and `additional_linker_inputs` do
+not provide that runtime linking interface.
